WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:14.880
The school 7F module is explicitly allocated this week. This session follows each of its six narrative sections, but explains mechanisms and decision links rather than copying the old companion’s environmental-emergency catalogue.
学校7F模块明确安排在本周。本课覆盖其全部六个叙述章节，但重点讲机制与决策联系，不照搬旧补充网站的环境急症目录。

00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:25.656
A mechanism helps you predict what might happen next. It does not identify the individual patient’s complete diagnosis, supply a missing treatment order or authorize a procedure.
机制知识帮助预测下一步可能发生什么，但不能确定患者的完整诊断、补足缺失治疗医嘱或授权操作。

00:00:25.656 --> 00:00:36.264
For any disagreement, preserve three labels: what the school source says, what current BCEHS guidance says, and what the actual licensed provider is authorized to do.
遇到差异时应保留三个标签：学校来源写了什么、BCEHS现行指导写了什么，以及实际执业者被授权做什么。

00:00:36.264 --> 00:00:50.976
Thermal energy disrupts cell membranes and proteins. Tissue injury triggers inflammation; when vascular permeability rises, fluid and proteins move from the intravascular space into surrounding tissues.
热能破坏细胞膜与蛋白质。组织损伤启动炎症；血管通透性升高时，液体与蛋白质会从血管内移向周围组织。

00:00:50.976 --> 00:01:03.456
The result can include swelling at the burn site and reduced effective circulating volume. Burn shock can combine vasodilation and capillary leak; it is not explained by skin appearance alone.
结果可能包括烧伤局部肿胀及有效循环血容量下降。烧伤休克可能同时包含血管扩张与毛细血管渗漏，不能只凭皮肤外观解释。

00:01:03.456 --> 00:01:14.472
The time course and body area matter, but a single percentage does not tell you current airway status, perfusion, depth, inhaled exposure or other trauma.
时间过程及受伤面积很重要，但单一百分比不能说明当前气道、灌注、深度、吸入暴露或其他创伤状况。

00:01:14.472 --> 00:01:26.208
The school calls the early response the ebb phase. Circulating volume and cardiac output may be reduced after a severe burn, limiting the delivery of oxygen and nutrients.
学校把早期反应称为ebb phase，即低潮期。严重烧伤后循环容量与心输出量可能下降，限制氧和营养输送。

00:01:26.208 --> 00:01:39.864
The later flow phase includes greater cardiac work and metabolic demand. Stress hormones and inflammation can sustain protein breakdown and increased energy needs long after the original exposure.
随后flow phase，即高潮期，包含更高的心脏做功和代谢需求。应激激素及炎症可使蛋白分解和能量需求在最初暴露后持续较长时间。

00:01:39.864 --> 00:01:54.336
The saved school text places the transition around forty-eight hours. A published burn primer describes a longer initial period. These are broad models, not a promise that every patient changes phase at one fixed hour.
学校存档文本把转变放在约48小时；发表的烧伤综述描述了更长的初始阶段。这些是概括模型，不表示每位患者都会在固定小时转换阶段。

00:01:54.336 --> 00:02:07.992
For a field assessment, ask when the injury happened and what care has occurred, then assess actual perfusion. Do not label new hypotension as normal ebb physiology or assume later tachycardia proves infection.
现场评估要了解受伤时间及既往处理，再检查实际灌注。不能把新发低血压当成正常低潮期，也不能认为后期心动过速就证明感染。

00:02:07.992 --> 00:02:23.088
Edema can distort anatomy. In a circumferential limb burn, swelling inside a relatively fixed skin boundary may reduce distal perfusion; in a circumferential chest burn, chest-wall expansion can be mechanically limited.
水肿会改变解剖结构。环周肢体烧伤中，固定皮肤范围内的肿胀可能减少远端灌注；环周胸部烧伤中，胸壁扩张也可能受机械限制。

00:02:23.088 --> 00:02:36.264
Inhaled hot gases, smoke and chemical irritants can injure upper or lower airways. Symptoms may evolve, so an early normal voice or oxygen reading does not guarantee a stable airway.
吸入热气体、烟雾及化学刺激物可损伤上、下气道；症状可能进展，因此早期声音正常或血氧读数正常，并不能保证气道稳定。

00:02:36.264 --> 00:02:49.224
Current BCEHS H10 emphasizes repeated airway-patency assessment, supplemental oxygen where indicated, and prompt reassessment when cough, voice change or soot suggests inhalation injury.
BCEHS现行H10强调反复评估气道通畅；有指征时给氧，并在咳嗽、声音变化或烟灰提示吸入损伤时及时复评。

00:02:49.224 --> 00:03:02.280
Above the vocal cords, heat injury can produce swelling and obstruction. New hoarseness, noisy inspiration or increasing effort needs attention even before the oxygen display falls.
声门以上的热损伤可造成肿胀与梗阻。新发声音嘶哑、吸气噪声或呼吸用力增加，即使血氧显示尚未下降，也需重视。

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:18.048
Below the vocal cords, smoke chemicals can injure the airway lining, impair clearance and provoke bronchospasm. Cough and wheeze point to different observations from a narrowed upper airway, but do not identify one cause by themselves.
声门以下，烟雾化学物可损伤气道内衬、妨碍清除并诱发支气管痉挛。咳嗽与哮鸣音不同于上气道狭窄的观察线索，但本身不能确定单一病因。

00:03:18.048 --> 00:03:33.096
Upper thermal and lower chemical injury are useful patterns, not absolute boundaries. The exposure, including steam or unusual chemicals, can change the pattern; an external facial burn does not describe the whole airway.
上部热损伤、下部化学损伤是有用模式，不是绝对分界。蒸汽或特殊化学物等暴露可改变模式；面部外观不能描述完整气道。

00:03:33.096 --> 00:03:51.096
Keep reassessing voice, airway sounds, effort, ventilation and circulation. Plan escalation before deterioration; advanced airway intervention belongs to appropriately trained and authorized clinicians, not to a decision based only on singed hair.
持续复评声音、气道音、呼吸做功、通气及循环。应在恶化前规划升级支援；高级气道干预由具备相应培训与授权的人员实施，不能只凭鼻毛烧焦决定。

00:03:51.096 --> 00:04:06.240
Carbon monoxide binds hemoglobin and impairs oxygen carriage. A standard two-wavelength pulse oximeter cannot reliably distinguish carboxyhemoglobin from oxyhemoglobin, so the displayed saturation may mislead.
一氧化碳会与血红蛋白结合并削弱氧输送。普通双波长脉搏血氧仪不能可靠区分碳氧血红蛋白与氧合血红蛋白，因此显示值可能误导。

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:18.312
A suspected combustion exposure is a history-and-scene problem as well as a monitor problem. Consider whether more than one person is affected and whether symptoms match the exposure.
疑似燃烧暴露既是病史与现场问题，也是监测问题。要考虑是否多人受影响，以及症状是否符合暴露情境。

00:04:18.312 --> 00:04:34.080
Current BCEHS J02 directs oxygen and consultation for suspected or confirmed CO. CO-oximetry, when available, can add information, but a device reading is not a universal mandatory screen or a stand-alone rule-out.
BCEHS现行J02对疑似或确诊CO暴露要求给氧并咨询。若可用，CO-oximetry可补充信息，但设备读数不是所有封闭火灾都必须做的通用筛查，也不能单独排除中毒。

00:04:34.080 --> 00:04:48.120
Think of oxygen transport as a delivery route. Carbon monoxide occupies hemoglobin binding sites and interferes with oxygen delivery and release. The usual pulse-oximeter number may not reveal that problem.
把氧运输看成配送路线。一氧化碳占据血红蛋白结合位点，并干扰氧输送及释放；普通血氧仪读数可能无法揭示这个问题。

00:04:48.120 --> 00:05:01.944
Cyanide acts further along the route by inhibiting mitochondrial energy production. Oxygen may reach a tissue that cannot use it normally. Combustion exposure can involve both poisons, as well as airway injury.
氰化物在路线后端抑制线粒体能量产生。氧可能已到组织，却无法正常利用。燃烧暴露可同时涉及两种毒物及气道损伤。

00:05:01.944 --> 00:05:16.344
Severe unexplained neurologic or circulatory decline after an enclosed fire raises concern, but no single bedside finding proves cyanide poisoning. A high lactate, if available, has other possible causes.
封闭火灾后无法解释的严重神经或循环恶化应引起警惕，但没有单一床旁发现能证明氰化物中毒。即使能测乳酸，升高也有其他可能原因。

00:05:16.344 --> 00:05:36.912
BCEHS J03 requires CliniCall consultation for suspected cyanide exposure. Its hydroxocobalamin monograph labels the antidote for CCP use. Recognize the concern, support the patient and communicate it; do not convert the school antidote mention into a PCP administration order.
BCEHS J03要求疑似氰化物暴露时咨询CliniCall。羟钴胺专论把解毒药标为CCP使用。应识别风险、支持患者并沟通，不能把学校提到解毒药当作PCP给药医嘱。

00:05:36.912 --> 00:05:49.872
Burn depth is not always obvious at first contact and can change in appearance. Ask about the mechanism, time, clothing, cooling already provided and possible inhalation exposure.
首次接触时烧伤深度未必明显，外观也可能变化。要了解机制、时间、衣物、此前降温及可能的吸入暴露。

00:05:49.872 --> 00:06:02.280
Rules of Nines and the patient’s hand can help estimate the area of partial-thickness or deeper burns. Do not count uncomplicated superficial redness in the BCEHS TBSA estimate.
九分法及患者手掌可帮助估算部分及更深烧伤面积。BCEHS的TBSA估算不计简单表浅红斑。

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:15.864
For children and irregular patterns, the appropriate chart and current local destination guidance matter. The percentage is an estimate for communication, not a precise measurement or automatic fluid formula.
儿童及形态不规则的烧伤需使用适当图表及当地转运指导。百分比是沟通估值，不是精确测量，也不是自动套用的输液公式。

00:06:15.864 --> 00:06:32.784
In this original practice case, a worker is already outside a smoke-filled equipment room. You find a small forearm burn, headache and a reassuring-looking saturation. Begin with scene safety and the primary survey, not with wound photography.
在这道原创练习中，工人已离开充满烟雾的设备间。你发现前臂小面积烧伤、头痛，血氧显示看似尚可。先做现场安全与初评，不是先拍伤口照片。

00:06:32.784 --> 00:06:48.336
During reassessment the voice becomes rough and breathing effort increases. Explain the change: the airway may be evolving independently of the visible skin injury. Reassess ventilation and prepare the appropriate support and escalation.
复评时声音变粗，呼吸做功增加。应解释为气道问题可能独立于可见皮肤损伤而进展。重评通气，准备适当支持及升级支援。

00:06:48.336 --> 00:07:03.600
The headache and exposure history also keep combustion toxicity on the problem list. A normal-looking conventional saturation cannot remove carbon monoxide from that list. Do not wait for a large skin burn or a device diagnosis.
头痛与暴露史还使燃烧毒物保留在问题清单中。普通血氧读数看似正常不能排除一氧化碳；不能等大面积皮肤烧伤或设备确诊才重视。

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:20.112
A useful pre-alert describes the enclosed-smoke exposure, the new voice change, breathing trend, circulation, treatment and response. State concern for inhalation injury and toxic exposure while acknowledging what remains unconfirmed.
有效预警要描述封闭烟雾暴露、新发声音改变、呼吸趋势、循环、处理及反应。应明确担忧吸入损伤与毒物暴露，同时说明哪些尚未证实。

00:07:20.112 --> 00:07:32.760
The core temperature reflects heat produced by metabolism and muscle work minus heat lost to the environment. Radiation, conduction, convection and evaporation all contribute.
核心体温取决于代谢与肌肉活动产生的热量，减去向环境散失的热量；辐射、传导、对流及蒸发都参与其中。

00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:47.976
Vasoconstriction and shivering can help conserve or produce heat. Sweating and skin blood flow can dissipate heat, but these responses have limits and depend on hydration, age, illness, clothing and air movement.
血管收缩与颤抖有助保存或产生热量；出汗及皮肤血流有助散热，但这些反应有极限，并受水合状态、年龄、疾病、衣着及气流影响。

00:07:47.976 --> 00:08:01.464
A hot or cold environment is not the only cause. Immobility, wet clothing, intoxication, illness, medications or a long extrication can defeat normal compensation.
冷热环境不是唯一原因。不能活动、衣物潮湿、中毒、疾病、药物或长时间脱困，都可能削弱正常代偿。

00:08:01.464 --> 00:08:14.760
Sweat cools mainly when it evaporates. In humid air, a person may be visibly soaked while losing heat poorly. The presence of sweat is therefore not evidence that temperature control is working.
汗液主要在蒸发时带走热量。潮湿空气中，即使全身湿透，散热也可能很差。因此，有汗不证明体温调节有效。

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:27.672
A wet patient on a cold surface can lose heat by contact, moving air and evaporation together. Covering the chest alone does not correct heat loss through the ground or an exposed wet back.
湿衣患者躺在冷表面，可同时经接触、流动空气及蒸发散热。只盖住胸部不能解决向地面或从湿背部散热的问题。

00:08:27.672 --> 00:08:40.944
Radiation and convection are heat-exchange processes, not always cooling processes. Direct sunlight or air hotter than the skin may add heat. Ask which direction the temperature gradient points.
辐射与对流是热交换过程，不总是在降温。直射阳光或比皮肤更热的空气可增加热量。要问温度梯度指向哪一边。

00:08:40.944 --> 00:08:57.960
Link each environmental observation to a practical control: safer shelter, shade, suitable clothing removal, insulation or active cooling. Then repeat the patient assessment; changing the environment does not prove that organ dysfunction has resolved.
把每项环境观察连接到实际控制：安全遮蔽、阴凉、适当移除衣物、隔热或主动降温。随后重复评估；环境改变不证明器官功能异常已解决。

00:08:57.960 --> 00:09:11.304
Heat illness exists on a spectrum. Cramps and heat exhaustion can progress; altered mental status or other central nervous system dysfunction in an overheated patient raises concern for heat stroke.
热病存在连续谱。热痉挛和热衰竭可进展；过热患者出现意识改变或其他中枢神经系统异常，应警惕热射病。

00:09:11.304 --> 00:09:23.520
Classic heat illness and exertional heat illness have different exposure contexts, but both can cause life-threatening organ injury. Sweating does not safely exclude exertional heat stroke.
经典热病与劳力性热病的暴露背景不同，但都可能造成危及生命的器官损伤；出汗并不能安全排除劳力性热射病。

00:09:23.520 --> 00:09:39.288
Current BCEHS I02 says begin cooling on scene where possible and continue during transport, with the method chosen around patient condition, movement safety and available resources. Do not treat environmental heat stroke with antipyretics.
BCEHS现行I02建议尽可能现场开始降温并在转运中继续；方法应兼顾患者状况、搬动安全及资源。环境性热射病不使用退热药治疗。

00:09:39.288 --> 00:09:54.840
A volunteer becomes confused during heavy work in a hot warehouse. The person is sweating. A forehead device reads thirty-eight point four degrees Celsius. Neither finding safely dismisses dangerous environmental heat illness.
志愿者在炎热仓库重体力活动时出现意识混乱，并有出汗。额温设备显示38.4摄氏度。这两项发现都不能安全排除危险环境热病。

00:09:54.840 --> 00:10:08.232
A surface reading is not a reliable substitute for the core measurement in the formal heat-stroke definition. Record the site and method, but do not wait for the display to cross forty before responding to the clinical threat.
表面读数不能可靠替代热射病正式定义中的核心测温。应记录部位及方法，但不能等显示值超过40才回应临床威胁。

00:10:08.232 --> 00:10:23.256
Start cooling and support airway, breathing and circulation while checking for competing or concurrent problems such as low glucose, infection or intoxication. Environmental heat and another emergency can coexist.
开始降温并支持气道、呼吸与循环，同时检查低血糖、感染或中毒等其他或并存问题。环境热病可与另一急症共存。

00:10:23.256 --> 00:10:39.024
BCEHS I02 calls for prompt cooling rather than antipyretics for environmental heat illness. Repeat mental status, breathing and perfusion during treatment. Oral water alone is not an effective substitute for full-body cooling.
BCEHS I02对环境热病要求及时降温，而非使用退热药。治疗期间复评意识、呼吸及灌注。只喝水不能有效替代全身降温。

00:10:39.024 --> 00:10:56.952
Heat exhaustion often includes weakness, dizziness, thirst and sweating without marked central nervous system impairment. New confusion, ataxia or reduced consciousness is a warning of more dangerous illness. Do not wait to settle the label before starting cooling.
热衰竭常有无力、头晕、口渴及出汗，而没有显著中枢神经系统异常。新发意识混乱、共济失调或意识下降，是更危险病情的警讯。不能等诊断名称确定才开始降温。

00:10:56.952 --> 00:11:10.584
Hypothermia is a core temperature below 35 degrees Celsius, but peripheral temperature readings can be inaccurate. Clinical stage and context are often more useful than claiming an exact core number in the field.
低体温定义为核心温度低于35摄氏度，但外周测温可能不准确。现场判断时，临床阶段及背景通常比声称精确核心温度更有用。

00:11:10.584 --> 00:11:24.168
Remove the person from ongoing cold exposure when safe, remove wet clothing, insulate and handle gently. Avoid unnecessary standing or rough movement in a markedly cold patient.
在安全前提下将患者移出持续寒冷环境，移除湿衣物、隔热并轻柔搬动。明显低温患者应避免不必要站立或粗暴移动。

00:11:24.168 --> 00:11:38.784
Shivering may disappear as illness worsens, but its absence alone does not stage the patient. Look for mental-status change, pulse and breathing trends, trauma, intoxication and other treatable causes.
病情加重时颤抖可能消失，但仅凭不颤抖不能完成分期。应观察意识、脉搏与呼吸趋势、创伤、中毒及其他可治疗原因。

00:11:38.784 --> 00:11:51.576
Cooling slows many cellular processes. A reduced heart rate in a deeply cold patient belongs in that context, but does not remove the need to assess perfusion and other causes of deterioration.
降温会减慢许多细胞过程。深度低温患者的心率下降应结合这一背景理解，但仍须评估灌注及其他恶化原因。

00:11:51.576 --> 00:12:04.248
The Osborn, or J, wave is a deflection near the end of the QRS complex that can occur with hypothermia. It is not unique to cold exposure and cannot supply an exact core temperature.
Osborn波，即J波，是QRS末端附近可见于低体温的偏移。它不是寒冷暴露特有表现，也不能提供准确核心温度。

00:12:04.248 --> 00:12:18.096
Clinical stage, environmental history and repeated findings matter when a thermometer is unreliable. A patient found on a floor indoors can be cold because another illness prevented movement or normal heat production.
测温不可靠时，临床阶段、环境史及重复发现很重要。室内倒地患者也可因其他疾病限制活动或产热而低温。

00:12:18.096 --> 00:12:34.320
Use gentle handling, prevent further heat loss and assess concurrent problems. If arrest is suspected, follow the actual current hypothermia and resuscitation pathway; do not invent a pulse-check interval by combining conflicting source versions.
应轻柔搬动、防止继续失热并评估并存问题。疑似停搏时遵循当前低温与复苏路径，不能把冲突版本的脉搏检查时间拼成新间隔。

00:12:34.320 --> 00:12:48.192
Drowning is a respiratory impairment process following submersion, not a special disease caused by saltwater alone. Aspiration can injure the alveolar surface and interfere with surfactant and normal expansion.
溺水是浸没后呼吸功能受损的过程，并非仅由盐水造成的特殊疾病。误吸可损伤肺泡表面，影响表面活性物质及正常扩张。

00:12:48.192 --> 00:13:01.656
Partly collapsed or fluid-filled regions receive less ventilation while blood continues to flow through them. This creates a ventilation-perfusion mismatch and shunt, so oxygenation can be difficult.
部分塌陷或充液区域通气减少，但血流仍经过，造成通气/灌注失衡及分流，因此氧合可能困难。

00:13:01.656 --> 00:13:16.344
A person who seems better immediately after rescue may later develop respiratory deterioration. Current BCEHS H12 emphasizes oxygenation, aspiration and heat-loss prevention, and conveyance for assessment.
刚获救时看似好转的人，之后仍可能出现呼吸恶化。BCEHS现行H12强调氧合、防误吸与防热量流失，并转运评估。

00:13:16.344 --> 00:13:28.560
Surfactant helps reduce surface tension so alveoli remain easier to keep open. Damage to that lining, edema and collapse can reduce the surface available for gas exchange.
表面活性物质帮助降低表面张力，使肺泡更容易保持开放。内衬损伤、水肿与塌陷可减少可用于气体交换的表面。

00:13:28.560 --> 00:13:41.160
If blood continues through a region receiving little or no fresh gas, it remains poorly oxygenated. That is the reason the school connects atelectasis, shunt and worsening hypoxemia.
若血液仍流经几乎没有新鲜气体进入的区域，就无法充分氧合。这就是学校把肺不张、分流与低氧血症加重联系起来的原因。

00:13:41.160 --> 00:13:57.624
The school diagram includes breath-holding, laryngospasm and aspiration. Treat this as a possible mechanism chain, not a required sequence in every drowning event. Do not wait for evidence of every step before supporting breathing.
学校图示包括屏气、喉痉挛及误吸。应把它视为可能的机制链，而非每次溺水必须依次出现的过程。不能等每个环节都有证据才支持呼吸。

00:13:57.624 --> 00:14:14.208
Current BCEHS H12 uses the same care principles for fresh and salt water. Oxygenation, ventilation when needed, thermal protection, reassessment and appropriate conveyance matter more than memorizing separate water-type algorithms.
现行BCEHS H12对淡水与海水采用相同照护原则。氧合、必要时通气、保温、复评与适当转运，比背两套水质算法更重要。

00:14:14.208 --> 00:14:26.184
Dysbaric illness relates to changing ambient pressure. During ascent, trapped gas expands; during a rapid pressure reduction, inert gas dissolved in tissue can form bubbles.
潜水压力病与环境压力变化有关。上升过程中被困气体会膨胀；压力快速下降时，组织内溶解的惰性气体可能形成气泡。

00:14:26.184 --> 00:14:39.048
Pulmonary barotrauma can cause pneumothorax or arterial gas embolism. Decompression illness can produce pain, sensory or motor changes, breathing difficulty or altered awareness.
肺气压伤可造成气胸或动脉气体栓塞；减压病可出现疼痛、感觉或运动异常、呼吸困难或意识改变。

00:14:39.048 --> 00:14:53.472
The dive profile and timing are essential history. Do not assume that every post-dive symptom is decompression sickness, and do not let a benign-looking skin examination overrule neurologic or respiratory deterioration.
潜水过程及发病时间是关键病史。不能假设每个潜水后症状都是减压病，也不能让皮肤外观正常压过神经或呼吸恶化。

00:14:53.472 --> 00:15:09.888
Imagine a free gas volume of one litre at two units of absolute pressure. At one unit, the simple Boyle model predicts two litres if temperature and gas amount stay constant. This is a teaching calculation, not a lung-volume target.
设想一团自由气体在2个绝对压力单位时为1升。在1个压力单位时，若温度和气体量不变，简单波义耳模型预测为2升。这是教学计算，不是肺容积目标。

00:15:09.888 --> 00:15:26.592
A lung cannot expand without limit. Trapped gas during ascent can injure tissue, whereas decompression sickness involves gas that was dissolved in tissues forming bubbles as pressure falls. The mechanisms are related to pressure but are not identical.
肺不可能无限膨胀。上升时被困气体可损伤组织；减压病则涉及原本溶于组织的气体在压力下降时形成气泡。两者都与压力有关，但机制不同。

00:15:26.592 --> 00:15:40.848
Decompression illness is the broader term covering decompression sickness and arterial gas embolism. A reported normal ascent or compliance with a dive computer does not exclude illness, and symptom patterns may overlap.
减压疾病是涵盖减压病及动脉气体栓塞的较广术语。报告上升正常或遵循潜水电脑，不能排除疾病；症状模式也可能重叠。

00:15:40.848 --> 00:15:58.752
Record dive depth and duration, breathing gas, repeated dives, ascent events and symptom times. New weakness, altered awareness or breathing difficulty requires urgent assessment and specialist coordination, even if symptoms improve after oxygen.
记录深度、时长、呼吸气体、重复潜水、上升事件及症状时间。新发无力、意识改变或呼吸困难需要紧急评估与专科协调，即使给氧后症状改善也一样。

00:15:58.752 --> 00:16:12.528
A diver who is short of breath may have lung barotrauma as well as other problems. Do not automatically borrow the CPAP approach used for selected drowning patients: the mechanisms and contraindications differ.
呼吸困难潜水者可能同时有肺气压伤及其他问题。不能自动套用某些溺水患者的CPAP方案；两者机制与禁忌不同。

00:16:12.528 --> 00:16:30.096
Current BCEHS I03 directs the highest possible oxygen percentage and flow for symptomatic patients, continuing even if symptoms resolve. Support inadequate ventilation with the trained airway and bag-mask pathway; assess breathing effectiveness repeatedly.
现行BCEHS I03对有症状患者要求尽可能高浓度及流量给氧，症状消失后仍继续。通气不足时按受训气道及球囊面罩路径支持，并反复检查呼吸有效性。

00:16:30.096 --> 00:16:44.664
I03 contraindicates CPAP and PEEP because underlying barotrauma may worsen. Keep the patient supine where possible, changing position when needed to protect the airway and respond to the clinical condition.
I03禁用CPAP及PEEP，因为可能加重潜在气压伤。可行时保持仰卧，必要时为保护气道及应对临床状况调整体位。

00:16:44.664 --> 00:16:58.008
Arrange emergency physician assessment and hyperbaric specialist coordination through the service pathway. Do not independently select a chamber destination or send a symptomatic diver back into the water.
应通过机构路径安排急诊医生评估及高压氧专科协调。不能自行选择高压舱目的地，也不能把有症状潜水者送回水下。

00:16:58.008 --> 00:17:30.432
The linked physiology video introduces several different effects. Nitrogen narcosis describes impaired function from breathing nitrogen at raised ambient pressure; it is not the same mechanism as bubbles in decompression sickness. Lung barotrauma can cause arterial gas embolism. These explanations can guide questions, but overlapping weakness, confusion or breathing difficulty after a dive requires urgent assessment and the current service pathway, not a diagnosis from one analogy.
链接生理视频介绍几种不同作用。氮麻醉描述高环境压力下呼吸氮气相关的功能受损，与减压病气泡机制不同；肺气压伤又可造成动脉气体栓塞。这些解释帮助提问，但潜水后无力、混乱或呼吸困难可能重叠，需紧急评估及现行机构路径，不能靠一个类比确诊。

00:17:30.432 --> 00:18:02.520
The video model does not establish fixed patient gas values. In Boyle’s model, volume changes while the gas amount remains fixed. Tissue uptake also depends on time. Carbon dioxide can accumulate if elimination is inadequate; dense breathing gas, workload and rebreathing are relevant despite the video’s reassuring statement. Record the actual dive and symptom history and support breathing. A chamber tour supplies neither a treatment table nor permission to operate equipment.
视频模型不确立患者固定气体数值。波义耳模型中，体积变化而气体量不变；组织摄取也取决于时间。二氧化碳清除不足可造成潴留；高密度呼吸气体、做功及再吸入仍相关，不能被视频安抚性说法排除。应记录真实潜水与症状史，并支持呼吸。高压舱参观既不提供治疗表，也不授权操作设备。

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:12.960
At high altitude the fraction of oxygen in air remains about the same, but barometric pressure is lower. The partial pressure driving oxygen into blood therefore falls.
高海拔空气中的氧比例大致不变，但气压下降，因此推动氧进入血液的氧分压降低。

00:18:12.960 --> 00:18:25.224
Ventilation and circulation can adapt over time. Acclimatization is not immediate, and a previously fit or experienced hiker can still develop serious altitude illness.
通气与循环可随时间适应，但适应并非立即完成；体能好或有经验的徒步者仍可能发生严重高原病。

00:18:25.224 --> 00:18:41.952
New ataxia or altered awareness suggests high-altitude cerebral edema; dyspnea at rest raises concern for high-altitude pulmonary edema. Current WMS guidance pairs urgent descent with oxygen when indicated rather than delaying one for the other.
新发共济失调或意识变化提示高原脑水肿；静息呼吸困难令人担忧高原肺水肿。WMS现行指导将紧急下降与有指征的氧疗并行，而不是等一个完成后才开始另一个。

00:18:41.952 --> 00:18:54.168
Crush injury begins with compressive force and local ischemia. Muscle cells lose membrane integrity and release intracellular material; injured tissue also becomes edematous.
挤压伤始于压迫力与局部缺血。肌细胞膜完整性受损并释放细胞内物质；受伤组织也会水肿。

00:18:54.168 --> 00:19:09.528
When compression is relieved, reperfusion may deliver potassium, myoglobin and other metabolites into the circulation. At the same time, injured muscle can retain fluid, worsening effective circulating-volume loss.
解除压迫后，再灌注可能将钾、肌红蛋白及其他代谢物带入循环；与此同时，受损肌肉可潴留液体，加重有效循环容量流失。

00:19:09.528 --> 00:19:21.240
The feared complications include dysrhythmia, acidosis, shock, kidney injury and later organ dysfunction. A patient may look stable before release and deteriorate afterward.
需警惕的并发症包括心律失常、酸中毒、休克、肾损伤及后续器官功能异常。患者解除压迫前可能看似稳定，之后却迅速恶化。

00:19:21.240 --> 00:19:37.464
Muscle cells need ATP, their usable energy supply, to maintain ion gradients. During prolonged ischemia, energy production falls and membrane control becomes impaired. Direct compression can damage the cell at the same time.
肌细胞需要ATP这一可用能量维持离子梯度。长时间缺血时，产能下降，细胞膜调控受损；直接压迫还可同时损坏细胞。

00:19:37.464 --> 00:19:52.056
Abnormal calcium handling activates damaging processes within the cell. As muscle breaks down, intracellular potassium, myoglobin and enzymes enter the surrounding fluid and may reach the circulation.
钙调控异常可激活细胞内损伤过程。肌肉分解时，细胞内钾、肌红蛋白及酶进入周围液体，并可能进入循环。

00:19:52.056 --> 00:20:09.600
Potassium affects cardiac electrical activity; myoglobin is associated with kidney injury; creatine kinase is a marker of muscle damage. These substances are not interchangeable, and a normal early ECG cannot measure the total burden of muscle injury.
钾影响心脏电活动；肌红蛋白与肾损伤有关；肌酸激酶是肌肉损伤指标。这些物质不能互换，早期ECG正常也不能测出肌肉损伤总量。

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:24.960
Swollen muscle also sequesters fluid, and shock reduces renal perfusion. Kidney injury is therefore not simply a pipe blocked by pigment; several linked processes matter. Do not wait for dark urine before recognizing the risk.
肿胀肌肉还会潴留液体，休克则减少肾灌注。因此肾损伤不只是色素堵住管道，而是多个相连过程。不能等尿液变深才识别风险。

00:20:24.960 --> 00:20:40.752
Entrapment duration, involved muscle mass, compressive force, access, temperature and associated trauma change the risk picture. Rescue work also introduces structural, electrical, machinery and secondary-collapse hazards.
受困时长、涉及肌肉量、压迫力、接近条件、温度及合并创伤都会改变风险；救援过程也可能出现结构、电力、机械及二次坍塌危险。

00:20:40.752 --> 00:20:55.104
The current BCEHS H02 calls for coordinated planning and CliniCall involvement for key pre-release treatment decisions. The lesson is to prepare a time-stamped plan and reassessment rather than improvise a fixed regimen.
BCEHS现行H02要求协调计划，并在关键解除前处理决策中联系CliniCall。本课重点是准备带时间记录的计划及复评，而不是临时编固定方案。

00:20:55.104 --> 00:21:09.720
Do not assume that every trapped patient needs the same fluid volume, that a tourniquet automatically prevents systemic effects, or that a fast unplanned release is harmless. Apply the current guideline and license-specific direction.
不能假设每位受困患者都需要相同液体量、止血带会自动防止全身效应，或快速无计划解除毫无风险。应依现行指南及执业层级指示行动。

00:21:09.720 --> 00:21:28.080
For significant crush injury, current BCEHS H02 includes considering two litres of normal saline immediately before release, with CliniCall consultation recommended for fluid planning. This is a source-specific consideration, not a fixed volume for every trapped limb.
对显著挤压伤，现行BCEHS H02包含考虑在解除前立即给予2升生理盐水，并建议咨询CliniCall制定补液计划。这是特定来源的考虑事项，不是每条被困肢体都要固定输入的量。

00:21:28.080 --> 00:21:43.032
The same guideline requires consultation before salbutamol for this indication. Calcium and other electrolyte treatments appear at different provider levels. Do not import the whole treatment list into an unsupervised PCP plan.
同一指南要求，为此适应症使用沙丁胺醇前必须咨询。钙及其他电解质治疗列于不同提供者级别，不能把整张处理清单搬进无督导的PCP计划。

00:21:43.032 --> 00:22:00.576
The school narrative says even a small amount of lactated Ringer solution can trigger immediate arrest in crush injury. That absolute is not supported by the AAST rhabdomyolysis consensus, which accepts either saline or lactated Ringer solution in its hospital context.
学校叙述称，挤压伤时即使少量乳酸林格液也可触发即时停搏。这一绝对说法不获AAST横纹肌溶解共识支持；该共识在其医院场景中接受盐水或乳酸林格液。

00:22:00.576 --> 00:22:15.336
This correction is not permission to switch the field fluid. Follow the current BC plan, consultation and patient-specific reassessment. Explain the local choice accurately without inventing a universal lethal mechanism.
这项修正不授权自行更换现场液体。应遵循现行BC计划、咨询及针对患者的复评。要准确解释本地选择，而不是编造通用致死机制。

00:22:15.336 --> 00:22:28.272
Muscle groups lie inside fascia that does not stretch freely. Bleeding or edema can raise pressure; rising compartment pressure reduces capillary perfusion and may injure nerve and muscle.
肌群位于不易伸展的筋膜室内。出血或水肿可升高压力；筋膜室压力上升会减少毛细血管灌注并损伤神经和肌肉。

00:22:28.272 --> 00:22:40.776
Worsening pain, a tense compartment, pain with passive stretch where assessed, sensory change or weakness can raise concern. No single finding rules the condition in or out.
疼痛加重、筋膜室紧张、评估时被动牵伸痛、感觉改变或无力都可能引起担忧；任何单一发现都不能独立确诊或排除。

00:22:40.776 --> 00:22:52.104
Distal pulses can remain present early because pressure sufficient to impair capillary flow may be lower than arterial pressure. Waiting for pulselessness risks late recognition.
早期远端脉搏仍可能存在，因为足以损害毛细血管血流的压力可能低于动脉压力。等到无脉才识别会造成延误。

00:22:52.104 --> 00:23:06.048
A muscle compartment contains tissue, nerves and vessels within a relatively unyielding fascial boundary. More volume inside raises pressure and can impair low-pressure venous drainage, making swelling worse.
肌肉筋膜室在相对不易扩张的筋膜边界内，容纳组织、神经及血管。内部容量增加会升高压力，妨碍低压静脉引流，并加重肿胀。

00:23:06.048 --> 00:23:22.656
The key is loss of the pressure gradient supporting tissue perfusion. Compartment pressure does not need to exceed systolic blood pressure before microvascular flow is threatened. A palpable artery farther down the limb does not demonstrate adequate muscle perfusion.
关键是维持组织灌注的压力梯度下降。筋膜室压力不必先超过收缩压，微血管血流就可能受威胁。肢体远端动脉可触及，并不证明肌肉灌注足够。

00:23:22.656 --> 00:23:39.792
Increasing pain, pain with passive movement, tense swelling and sensory or motor changes raise concern. Findings can be incomplete, especially when consciousness or communication is impaired. No single sign safely excludes the problem.
疼痛增加、被动活动痛、紧张肿胀及感觉或运动变化应引起担忧。意识或沟通受限时，体征可能不完整。没有单一体征可以安全排除问题。

00:23:39.792 --> 00:23:56.040
Repeat and time-stamp the examination, document analgesia and response, and seek urgent escalation. Hospital pressure measurement and surgical decisions are not replaced by a field pulse check or a fixed number of hours assumed to be safe.
应重复检查并标记时间，记录镇痛及反应，紧急升级处理。现场触脉或假定安全的固定小时数，不能替代医院测压与手术决策。

00:23:56.040 --> 00:24:09.384
Crush syndrome describes a systemic pathophysiologic risk associated with significant muscle compression and release. Compartment syndrome describes pressure-related ischemia in a confined anatomical space.
挤压综合征描述显著肌肉受压及解除后相关的全身病理生理风险；筋膜室综合征描述局限解剖空间内因压力导致的缺血。

00:24:09.384 --> 00:24:22.680
They may coexist, but one does not prove the other. Crush release can produce systemic electrolyte and volume problems; a compartment may threaten a limb even without a dramatic systemic presentation.
两者可能同时存在，但一个不能证明另一个。挤压解除可引发全身电解质和容量问题；即使没有明显全身表现，筋膜室也可能威胁肢体。

00:24:22.680 --> 00:24:34.296
Useful handover describes mechanism, duration, changes in pain or perfusion, interventions and release time. Do not replace serial findings with a single label.
有效交接要描述机制、持续时间、疼痛或灌注变化、已实施处理及解除时间。不能用单一标签替代连续观察。

00:24:34.296 --> 00:24:51.000
In this original rehearsal, a person has a thigh pinned beneath equipment. Before coordinated release the patient is awake, with tense swelling and a pressure of one hundred eighteen over seventy-four. That initial pressure does not make release risk disappear.
在这道原创演练中，患者大腿被设备压住。协调解除前，患者清醒、肢体紧张肿胀，血压118/74。这个初始血压不能消除解除风险。

00:24:51.000 --> 00:25:08.952
After release, the pulse is one hundred twenty-four, pressure is ninety-four over sixty, and the patient is more drowsy. First respond to the deteriorating patient and reassess the primary survey; do not spend the transition arguing over one diagnostic label.
解除后脉搏124、血压94/60，患者更嗜睡。先回应恶化患者并重新初评，不要把关键转变时间用来争论某个诊断标签。

00:25:08.952 --> 00:25:25.968
Consider volume loss, electrolyte disturbance and acidosis alongside bleeding, chest injury, hypoxia and other causes. Report the concern for crush-related deterioration, but do not claim a potassium result from a monitor waveform alone.
在失血、胸部损伤、缺氧及其他原因之外，还要考虑容量丢失、电解质异常和酸中毒。报告挤压相关恶化担忧，但不能只凭监护波形声称已知血钾结果。

00:25:25.968 --> 00:25:42.288
Hand over the estimated compression time and muscle region, exact release time, serial findings, care before and after release, consultation and response. That timeline is more useful than saying only that the patient has crush syndrome.
交接预计受压时间、肌肉区域、确切解除时间、连续发现、解除前后处理、咨询及反应。这条时间线比只说患者有挤压综合征更有用。

00:25:42.288 --> 00:25:56.448
Capillary leak describes increased movement of fluid and proteins out of vessels. Hypoxemia describes low arterial oxygen; cyanosis, confusion or a low saturation can have several causes.
毛细血管渗漏指液体及蛋白从血管外移增加；低氧血症指动脉血氧低。发绀、意识混乱或血氧读数低都可能有多种原因。

00:25:56.448 --> 00:26:06.600
Reperfusion is restored blood flow after ischemia; it can restore oxygen delivery while also carrying accumulated cellular contents into circulation.
再灌注是缺血后血流恢复；它能恢复供氧，也可能将积聚的细胞内容物带入循环。

00:26:06.600 --> 00:26:18.744
Third-spacing is a conceptual way to describe fluid that is no longer effectively available to the circulating volume. It is not a precise bedside measurement or an independent fluid order.
第三间隙是描述液体不再有效参与循环容量的概念性术语；它不是精确床旁测量，也不是独立输液医嘱。

00:26:18.744 --> 00:26:31.824
SIRS means systemic inflammatory response syndrome. Major burns or other severe injuries can produce systemic inflammation without infection. A rapid pulse and fever alone do not prove sepsis.
SIRS指全身炎症反应综合征。重大烧伤或其他严重损伤，即使没有感染，也可造成全身炎症。单有脉快和发热不能证明脓毒症。

00:26:31.824 --> 00:26:47.328
ARDS means acute respiratory distress syndrome. Inflammatory damage to the lung barrier can cause edema and poor gas exchange. It is not a name for every low saturation or a diagnosis made from one field finding.
ARDS指急性呼吸窘迫综合征。肺屏障的炎症损伤可造成水肿和气体交换不良。它不是每次低血氧的统称，也不能凭一项现场发现诊断。

00:26:47.328 --> 00:27:03.216
Hyperkalemia means elevated potassium in blood. That can disturb cardiac conduction, but an ECG is not a potassium assay. Connect the crush history to monitoring and urgent support rather than claiming a laboratory value you have not measured.
高钾血症指血钾升高，可扰乱心脏传导，但ECG不是血钾检测。应把挤压病史连到监测及紧急支持，不能声称知道尚未测量的实验室数值。

00:27:03.216 --> 00:27:17.520
Fasciotomy is a surgical opening of fascia to decompress an affected compartment when indicated. Your learning task is recognition, reassessment and timely escalation, not attempting a field surgical release.
筋膜切开术是在有指征时通过手术切开筋膜，为受影响筋膜室减压。学习任务是识别、复评和及时升级，不是在现场尝试外科切开。

00:27:17.520 --> 00:27:34.080
The Week 9 outline calls descent an absolute first priority before oxygen or medication, and calls CO-oximetry mandatory for every enclosed fire. Those statements are retained as school prompts but should not be taught as universal clinical rules.
第9周纲要把下降描述为在氧疗或药物前绝对优先，并称每个封闭火灾都必须做CO-oximetry。这些内容作为学校提示保留，但不能教成通用临床规则。

00:27:34.080 --> 00:27:50.160
Current altitude guidance treats urgent descent and indicated oxygen as complementary actions. Current BCEHS J02 calls for oxygen and consultation for suspected carbon monoxide exposure; standard pulse oximetry may mislead.
现行高原指导将紧急下降与有指征的氧疗视为并行措施。BCEHS现行J02对疑似一氧化碳暴露要求给氧并咨询；普通脉搏血氧读数可能误导。

00:27:50.160 --> 00:28:03.792
For written exams, ask which dated school revision is assessed. For clinical learning, use current BCEHS guidance and authorized scope; do not merge conflicting statements into a compromise algorithm.
备考时要核实学校考核的是哪一版文件。临床学习应遵循BCEHS现行指南及授权范围；不能把冲突内容折中拼成混合算法。
